## 1. 🌈 Colour Palette

Our colour system has four layers: **Cosmic Void** (backgrounds), **Purple Core** (brand identity), **SA Accents** (flag colours, visible and proud), and **Indian Ocean Teal** (secondary accent).

### Cosmic Void — Backgrounds & Surfaces

Deep purple-black backgrounds inspired by the Karoo night sky. Darker and richer than the old system — the void has visible purple depth.

| Token | Hex | Used For |
|-------|-----|----------|
| `--cosmic-void` / `--void` | `#0D001A` | Primary page background. Deep space with purple undertone |
| `--void-elevated` / `--pretoria-blue` | `#1A0A2E` | Card, panel, and sidebar backgrounds — rich dark plum |
| `--void-surface` | `#24103A` | Elevated surfaces: dropdowns, modals, tooltips |
| `--void-hover` | `#2E1A45` | Hover states on dark surfaces, button backgrounds |

### Purple Core — Brand Identity

The purple system has been restructured. **Purple Core (#6B21A8)** is the deeper, more sophisticated primary brand color. **Neon Glow (#A855F7)** is reserved as a sparing accent for CTAs and highlights. Old `--neon-grape` (#9D4EDD) is kept as a compatibility alias.

| Token | Hex | Used For |
|-------|-----|----------|
| `--purple-core` | `#6B21A8` | **NEW primary brand colour.** CTAs, buttons, links, brand marks |
| `--neon-grape` | `#9D4EDD` | **ALIAS** — kept for legacy component compatibility |
| `--neon-glow` | `#A855F7` | **NEW sparing accent.** Used only for CTAs and careful highlights |
| `--grape-light` | `#C084FC` | Hover states on primary elements, highlighted text |
| `--grape-dim` | `#581C87` | Active/pressed states, secondary purple elements |
| `--grape-subtle` | `rgba(157, 78, 221, 0.15)` | Soft purple backgrounds, badges, selection highlights |
| `--grape-glow` | `rgba(168, 85, 247, 0.35)` | Glow aura — used in shadows and backdrop effects |
| `--electric-indigo` | `#4C1D95` | Deep purple for dark gradients, secondary brand surfaces |
| `--hyper-crimson` | `#FF2A6D` | **Accent pop.** Used sparingly for notifications, alerts, decorative energy — never on CTAs |

### Indian Ocean Teal — Secondary Accent

Shifted from electric blue-teal to a warmer, nature-inspired teal. Think Indian Ocean at sunrise, or the silver leaves of Table Mountain's native trees.

| Token | Hex | Used For |
|-------|-----|----------|
| `--joburg-teal` | `#00D4AA` | Secondary CTAs, interactive accents, active states, link hover |
| `--teal-dim` | `#00A887` | Pressed/active states on teal elements |
| `--teal-subtle` | `rgba(0, 212, 170, 0.15)` | Teal-tinted backgrounds, info badges |

### SA Accents — Flag Colours (Visible and Proud)

Unlike the old system (where these were buried as semantic badge colors), the SA flag colours are now **design elements** visible in gradients, stripes, dividers, and decorative elements.

| Token | Hex | SA Flag Meaning | Used For |
|-------|-----|-----------------|----------|
| `--sa-green` / `--mzansi-green` | `#007749` | The land and agriculture | Success states, gradient stripes, decorative patterns, flag elements |
| `--sa-gold` / `--mzansi-gold` | `#FFB81C` | Natural wealth and sunshine | Premium features, gold glow, achievement badges, accent gradients |
| `--sa-red` / `--mzansi-red` | `#E03C31` | The struggle and sacrifice | Error states, flag stripes, decorative section elements |
| `--sa-blue` / `--mzansi-blue` | `#002C6F` | The sky and oceans | Info states, flag segments, deep gradient blends |

### Neutrals — Text & Borders

| Token | Hex | Used For |
|-------|-----|----------|
| `--text-primary` | `#F5F0FF` | Primary text (near-white with violet warmth) |
| `--text-secondary` | `#C4B0D4` | Body text, descriptions, metadata |
| `--text-tertiary` | `#8B7D98` | Placeholder text, disabled states, subtle labels |
| `--text-quaternary` | `#5C4F68` | Footnotes, timestamps, de-emphasized text |
| `--border-default` | `#2A1A3E` | Standard card/input borders |
| `--border-subtle` | `#1E1030` | Ultra-thin dividers |
| `--border-hover` | `#4A2570` | Hover borders on interactive elements |
| `--border-active` | `#A855F7` | Active/focus borders |

### Colour Aliases (Backward Compatibility)

The following old token names are preserved as aliases so existing components continue to work without modification:

| Old Token | Now Maps To |
|-----------|-------------|
| `--neon-grape` | `#9D4EDD` (kept as alias, not primary) |
| `--mzansi-green` | `#007749` (same as `--sa-green`) |
| `--mzansi-gold` | `#FFB81C` (same as `--sa-gold`) |
| `--mzansi-red` | `#E03C31` (same as `--sa-red`) |
| `--mzansi-blue` | `#002C6F` (same as `--sa-blue`) |
| `--pretoria-blue` | `#1A0A2E` (now maps to void-elevated) |
| `--glass-border` | `rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08)` (kept for glass card compat) |

