## 8. 📱 Quick Reference — By Element

| Element | Background | Text | Border | Radius |
|---------|-----------|------|--------|--------|
| Page body | `--cosmic-void (#0D001A)` | `--text-primary` | — | — |
| Premium card | `--void-elevated` gradient | `--text-primary` | `--border-default` | 16px |
| Inset card | Darker gradient | `--text-primary` | `--border-subtle` | 16px |
| Glass card | Purple-teal tint + blur | `--text-primary` | `rgba(168,85,247,0.12)` | 16px |
| Primary button | `--purple-core (#6B21A8)` | white | none | 8px |
| Neon glow button | `--neon-glow (#A855F7)` | white | glow-purple | 8px |
| Ghost button | transparent | `--text-primary` | `--border-default` | 8px |
| Input | `rgba(255,255,255,0.03)` | `--text-primary` | `--border-default` | 8px |
| Modal | `--void-surface` | `--text-primary` | `--border-default` | 16px |
| Badge (purple) | `--grape-subtle` | `--grape-light` | none | 6px |
| Top nav | `rgba(13,0,26,0.8)` + blur | `--text-secondary` | `--border-subtle` | — |
| Sidebar | `--void-elevated (#1A0A2E)` | `--text-secondary` | `--border-subtle` | — |

---

## 9. ✅ What Makes New PGS Different From Every Other Dark SaaS

You know you're looking at Purple Glow Social when:

1. **The background is cosmic void** — deep purple-black (`#0D001A`), referencing the Karoo night sky, not generic flat black
2. **SA flag colours are visible design elements** — green, gold, red, blue appear in gradients, stripes, section dividers, and decorative patterns. They're not hidden away as semantic badge colours
3. **The purple has depth** — `#6B21A8` (Purple Core) is sophisticated, not garish. The old `#9D4EDD` (Neon Grape) only appears for legacy compatibility
4. **Geometric patterns** — Ndebele-inspired dot grids and diagonal lines add texture and cultural resonance
5. **Noise texture** — a subtle grain overlay across the entire page (`.noise-overlay`), giving warmth and film-like depth
6. **Flag stripe dividers** — section transitions that celebrate the SA flag (`.flag-stripe`, `.divider-flag`)
7. **Borders have colour** — our borders (`#2A1A3E`, `#1E1030`) are actual purple-hued colours, not just white opacity
8. **Multi-layer glow system** — dedicated purple, teal, and gold glow classes for different contexts
9. **Three card styles** — Premium (elevated depth), Inset (sinks in), Glass (blur backdrop) — each with a purpose
10. **Nature-inspired teal** — `#00D4AA` (warm coastal teal) replaces the generic electric blue-teal
11. **Syne headlines are bold** — our display font commands attention
12. **The tone is SA-warm** — friendly, helpful, proud but not pushy

---

## 10. 🙅 Do's and Don'ts

### ✅ Do
- Use `--purple-core` (#6B21A8) for all primary CTAs
- Use `--neon-glow` (#A855F7) **sparingly** — only for high-impact conversion actions
- Use `--cosmic-void` (#0D001A) as the main page background
- Use `--text-primary` (#F5F0FF) for headings — never pure white
- Use SA flag colours in decorative elements (gradients, stripes, patterns) — they're part of our identity now
- Add `.noise-overlay` to the page body for the signature grain texture
- Use `.flag-stripe` as a subtle section divider
- Use `.pattern-dots` for decorative backgrounds on hero or feature sections
- Apply glow effects on hero sections and primary CTAs
- Use `glass-card` for premium/featured content, `premium-card` for standard content, `inset-card` for secondary content

### ❌ Don't
- Use pure black (#000000) for backgrounds
- Use pure white (#FFFFFF) for text
- Use SA flag colours ONLY as semantic badges — they're design elements now
- Use corporate jargon in copy ("leverage", "utilise", "synergise")
- Make buttons pill-shaped (9999px radius) — use 8px radius consistently
- Use the old `neon-grape` (#9D4EDD) as the primary brand colour — that's `purple-core` now
- Use flat blur circles for glow — use the multi-layer glow classes instead
- Use drop shadows on dark surfaces — use glow and background elevation instead
- Overuse patterns — one pattern per section maximum

---

## 11. 🔄 Migration Guide — From Old to New

If you're updating existing PGS pages to the new design system:

| Old Style | New Style |
|-----------|-----------|
| `#05040A` (void) bg | `#0D001A` (cosmic-void) — deeper |
| `#0A0815` (void-elevated) bg | `#1A0A2E` (void-elevated) — richer plum |
| `#9D4EDD` (neon-grape) primary | `#6B21A8` (purple-core) — deeper brand purple |
| `#00E0FF` (joburg-teal) | `#00D4AA` (joburg-teal) — nature-inspired |
| `#FFCC00` (mzansi-gold old) | `#FFB81C` (sa-gold) — brighter, warmer |
| `#007A4D` (mzansi-green old) | `#007749` (sa-green) — bolder |
| `#DE3831` (mzansi-red old) | `#E03C31` (sa-red) — more visible |
| `#002395` (mzansi-blue old) | `#002C6F` (sa-blue) — deeper |
| `rgba(255,255,255,0.08)` borders | `#2A1A3E` (border-default) — coloured borders |
| `rgba(255,255,255,0.05)` borders | `#1E1030` (border-subtle) — coloured subtle |
| `bg-neon-grape` | Use `bg-purple-core` for primary, `bg-neon-glow` sparingly |
| `aerogel-card` class | Still works (kept as `.aerogel-card` alias) |
| `glow-text` class | Still works (kept as alias; prefer `.glow-text-purple`) |
| `animate-enter` class | Still works (kept as alias; prefer `.animate-fade-up`) |

---

## 12. 🔧 Custom Utility Classes

### Pattern & Texture Classes
- `.noise-overlay` — Subtle SVG grain texture overlay on the page
- `.pattern-dots` — Ndebele-inspired purple dot grid
- `.pattern-dots-teal` — Teal dot grid
- `.pattern-dots-gold` — Gold dot grid
- `.pattern-lines` — Diagonal purple lines
- `.pattern-lines-teal` — Diagonal teal lines
- `.pattern-lines-gold` — Diagonal gold lines

### Flag Classes
- `.flag-stripe` — Horizontal SA flag colour stripe
- `.flag-stripe-vertical` — Vertical SA flag stripe
- `.flag-accent` — Thin decorative SA flag gradient line
- `.border-sa-flag` — Card border with SA flag gradient

### Divider Classes
- `.divider-wave` — Wavy SVG-based section divider
- `.divider-slant` — Diagonal section divider
- `.divider-flag` — Section divider using flag colours

### Card Classes
- `.premium-card` — Elevated card with depth and purple edge glow
- `.inset-card` — Card that sinks into background
- `.glass-card` — Glassmorphism with purple-tinted border
- `.aerogel-card` — Legacy alias for glass-card

### Glow Classes
- `.glow-purple` — Multi-layer purple box glow
- `.glow-teal` — Multi-layer teal box glow
- `.glow-gold` — Multi-layer gold box glow
- `.glow-subtle` — Faint ambient purple glow
- `.glow-text-purple` — Purple text shadow glow
- `.glow-text-gold` — Gold text shadow glow
- `.glow-text-teal` — Teal text shadow glow
- `.glow-text` — Legacy alias (maps to simplified purple glow)
- `.glow-orb-purple` — Large blurry purple decorative orb
- `.glow-orb-teal` — Large blurry teal decorative orb
- `.glow-orb-gold` — Large blurry gold decorative orb

### Animation Classes
- `.animate-fade-up` — Scroll-reveal fade with upward motion
- `.animate-stagger` — For staggered children (supports up to 8)
- `.animate-float` — Gentle floating animation (decorative elements)
- `.animate-pulse-glow` — Pulsing purple glow effect
- `.animate-pulse-glow-teal` — Pulsing teal glow effect
- `.animate-spin-slow` — Slow spin (8s)
- `.animate-slide-up` — Slide up with fade
- `.animate-scale-in` — Scale in with fade
- `.animate-enter` — Legacy enter animation (kept for compat)

### Text Gradient Classes
- `.text-gradient-purple` — Purple-to-violet gradient text
- `.text-gradient-gold` — Gold gradient text
- `.text-gradient-sa` — SA flag colour gradient text
- `.text-gradient-teal` — Teal gradient text

### Background Gradient Classes
- `.bg-gradient-sa` — SA flag colour gradient background
- `.bg-gradient-purple-teal` — Purple to teal gradient background

---

*This design system is a living document. As PGS grows, these tokens may evolve — but the soul stays the same: cosmic purple glow, South African pride, and AI that helps real people.*

*Last updated: June 2026 — Design System 2.0 (non-generic, culturally distinctive)*
